Hi Avery,

You're a workspace owner, which usually means you're in every channel. A few settings that founders tell us made the biggest difference:

1. Set a notification schedule. Slack goes quiet outside 8am to 7pm unless someone uses your name.
2. Turn on VIPs. Pick the five people whose messages should always come through.
3. Mute #random and every #social-* channel. You can still read them; they just stop pinging.
4. Use "Later" instead of leaving messages unread. Save it, set a reminder, clear the badge.
5. Ask Slack AI for a daily recap of the channels you muted.

Try one this week: https://email.slack.com/l/focus-tips-0911

